e between telling parents when they ask, notifying parents, and requiring parental permission for a new name or pronouns.\n- **His records:**\n  - **H.R. 5 (2023), House Aye:** a multi-subject bill. His House record counts as the same legislature, but at this level a record still can't seat a chair.\n  - **S. 2702, which he sponsored:** I coded it `chair-shaped` on the permission rung (it requires \"express parental consent\" before staff affirm a different identity). It still can't seat a chair here, because it is a record and not his words.\n- **Choice a reviewer might dispute:** Banks says \"This bill makes sure schools can't push radical gender ideology behind parents' backs\". You could argue that saying this makes the bill's text his position, the way Maloy's \"would have voted yes\" made the RFMA's text hers. I didn't read it that way, because his words never mention parental permission or notification.\n- **needs_source:** his own first-person statement on whether schools must notify parents or get their permission before staff use a different name or pronouns.\n- **Quote:** the \"kept in the dark\" line is tiered `direction` and marked quotable.","ttft_ms":30220,"type":"result","duration_ms":50674,"uuid":"da31db3d-3597-4652-b2b7-bf70d741b09f","ttft_stream_ms":6933,"time_to_request_ms":82,"first_content_frame_ms":6933,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
